    <summary type="text">Jellyfin brings in ratings and allows you to set custom ratings for shows, which is nice for things like &#34;block anything worse than TV-14 for my kid&#39;s...</summary>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Jellyfin brings in ratings and allows you to set custom ratings for shows,&#xA;which is nice for things like &amp;ldquo;block anything worse than TV-14 for my kid&amp;rsquo;s&#xA;account&amp;rdquo;. But what if my firend&amp;rsquo;s kids can watch shows I don&amp;rsquo;t want my kids&#xA;watching? Turns out tags exist and are great!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;tag-the-content&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;heading-wear-glyph&#34;&gt;Tag the content&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#tag-the-content&#34; class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First is to actually tag the content - in the UI it&amp;rsquo;s simple.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Login with admin&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Manage Metadata&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Click the content you want to tag and find the &lt;code&gt;Tags&lt;/code&gt; section&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Add your tag&amp;hellip; for example &lt;code&gt;blocked:girls&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;filter-on-the-account&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;heading-wear-glyph&#34;&gt;Filter on the account&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#filter-on-the-account&#34; class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Go to &lt;code&gt;Dashboard&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;Users&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;Library Access&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;Parental Control&lt;/code&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;Block items with tags&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;</content>
